<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened Runtime entitlements for the Developer ID build.

  Notarization requires the Hardened Runtime, and the Hardened Runtime blocks
  several things by default. This file re-enables the minimum needed and
  nothing else.

  DELIBERATELY ABSENT, and each one should stay absent unless a signed build
  actually proves it necessary:

    com.apple.security.app-sandbox
        Swept reads other applications' caches, ~/Library/Logs, browser
        profiles and LaunchAgents. No sandbox entitlement makes that possible,
        which is the reason this app is not on the Mac App Store at all
        (docs/LEGAL.md). Adding it here would break every scanner.

    com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
        Lets the process load libraries signed by anyone. Swept loads no
        plug-ins and no external binaries, so it has no reason to. Widely
        cargo-culted into Tauri entitlement files; do not copy it in without a
        crash log that names library validation as the cause.

    com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
        Strictly broader than allow-jit below, and blunter. If the webview
        turns out to need something, try it only after allow-jit has been
        proven insufficient.

    com.apple.security.automation.apple-events
        Only needed to drive other apps. Disposal goes through NSFileManager's
        trashItem (the `trash` crate's default path on macOS), not Finder
        Apple Events, so nothing here sends one.

  UNVERIFIED UNTIL THE FIRST SIGNED BUILD: allow-jit below is included because
  WKWebView's JavaScript engine may need it in the host process. It is the
  narrow, correct entitlement for JIT and does not weaken the runtime the way
  the two alternatives above do. If a *notarized* build launches cleanly
  without it, take it out — see docs/RELEASING.md, "Verifying the signed build".
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
